# What `gcloud run deploy --source streamlit` must not upload to the Cloud Build
# staging bucket.
#
# This file exists separately from .dockerignore because gcloud does not read
# that one. Without a .gcloudignore, gcloud derives its defaults from a
# .gitignore IN THIS DIRECTORY — and there is none; the repository's lives one
# level up and is never consulted. So a filled-in .streamlit/secrets.toml, which
# .dockerignore now keeps out of the image, would still be uploaded to a bucket
# on every deploy, carrying the service_role key that bypasses every row-level
# security policy in the schema.
#
# Keep in step with .dockerignore.

.streamlit/secrets.toml
**/secrets.toml

.env
.env.*

.venv
venv

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache

.DS_Store
